14. `Before the attack, the administrator configured Windows to capture command line details in the event logs. What command did they run to achieve this?`
	1. Inside `C:\Users\Puter\Downloads\EnduringEcho\C\Users\Administrator\AppData\Roaming\Microsoft\Windows\PowerShell\PSReadline` there is the file `ConsoleHost_history.txt` which is the logs for the administrator account. Here we can see that a registry key was added to watch the command line.
- Flag #14 -> `reg add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\System\Audit" /v ProcessCreationIncludeCmdLine_Enabled /t REG_DWORD /d 1 /f`

